WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.002
-You said that you're having
an amazing week.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.070
-It's been the craziest week.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.471
Yeah, so, I just got back
from L.A.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.707
and I got to tour
"The Brady Bunch" house.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.842
It's been renovated.
-No, I'm freaking out.

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:11.845
I know everything about it.
I'm watching the show right now.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.846
"The Brady Bunch" -- They
got all the --

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.281
They got all the Brady Bunch
together with, like,

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.116
the HGTV superstars
and made the house.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.052
-There's all this,
like, old stuff.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.087
I got to use a rotary phone.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.189
By the way,
those things are cool.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:27.260
Have you used one of those?
You know, the rotary phone.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.961
It was like --
You have to press the button

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.096
and then turn the dial.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.830
-You don't press
any buttons at all.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.067
You put four finger in a hole
and then you --

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:37.736
-I got tired just --
-Press the buttons. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:39.372
You're such a kid.
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.040
[ Australian accent ] They had
crazy things.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.875
They had stairs
you would walk up.

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:44.377
-It was crazy.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.412
-But you did walk up the
classic stairs.

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:47.480
-The classic stairs.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.581
-You and your family
did the pose.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.250
-It was legendary.
-Look at this.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.986
This is the Irwins at
"The Brady Bunch" house.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:55.088
-All I could think was the theme
song just rolling in my head.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.991
-Dude, that's legendary!
-How awesome is that?

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.959
It was so cool.
-I want to check it out.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.260
I love it.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.363
I know -- We were talking
backstage about live stuff.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.831
And you've been on our show
a bunch of times.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.400
But you said they kind of
squeaked out of you.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.969
that you're a super-fan of
"Saturday Night Live."

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:13.039
-Oh, I love "SNL," so it's so
cool, I mean, to be on the show

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.774
with Colin and with Michael
and you, of course.

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:20.480
Like, I've always -- Like,
growing up --

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.383
-You could have started with me.

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:26.318
-Yeah, sorry about that.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:28.721
-Your cowbell sketch
and all those.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.090
I love it. I love it.
I really do.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.324
I really, really do.

00:01:32.324 --> 00:01:34.727
-I want to talk about --
'Cause I love your family.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:35.995
I see them all the time.
They're here.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.297
Bindi got engaged.
-She did.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:39.932
-This is amazing to me.
-Yeah, Bindi just got engaged.

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:42.035
[ Cheers and applause ]
How awesome is that?

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.871
-Now, Bindi got engaged
at the zoo.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.205
-She did.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.340
Yeah, so, it was right at the
Australia Zoo gardens.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.042
Chandler, who's now
her fiancé --

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:51.043
-I know Chandler, yeah.

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:52.312
-He's the loveliest guy.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.480
He's so loyal
and so kind to Bindi.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.182
So it was amazing.
Look at this. They took a photo.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.283
-How beautiful is that?

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.618
Yeah, I got to
photograph it, too.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:01.187
It was incredible.
-You take great photos.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.822
-Oh, thank you.
Thank you very much.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.957
-This thing made me laugh,
because -- You sent me this.

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:06.291
I go, "That is gorgeous."

00:02:06.291 --> 00:02:08.861
And you're like, "Actually,
since I took the photo,

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:11.230
I wanted to rehearse where
exactly everyone would stand."

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.166
-So, before we did it,
Chandler came up to me,

00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:15.368
and, you know, of course
he asked Mom and I,

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.502
asked our permission,
but he also said,

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:17.904
"I want to make sure
it's perfect,

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.239
where we're doing this --
where I'm doing this proposal."

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:22.808
So, I stood in for Bindi
and mocked up

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:25.144
where he was going to propose.

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:28.547
And Bindi hasn't even seen this
photo, but I've got it with me.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:33.786
So, this is me. It was awesome.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.529
It was the happiest moment
of my life.

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:46.032
-Oh, I love you.
I love you, man.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.667
And, so, you are making plans
after the wedding.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.302
Is it gonna be at the zoo?

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:51.470
-Oh, it's going to be
at the zoo.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:52.905
I'm walking Bindi
down the aisle,

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.907
which is just gonna be awesome.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:58.344
But I've got some big ideas
for the wedding

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.812
that I've broached with Bindi.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.114
Like, first of all,
right off the bat,

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:03.483
Idris Elba deejaying.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.584
-Absolutely.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.285
That's the best idea --
Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:07.553
Go big or go home.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.021
-And then I thought, you know,
you need something

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:10.222
that people are gonna remember,

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:11.791
so I'm thinking
rappelling out of choppers.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.859
Like, Bindi, Chandler
both come out of choppers,

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:15.395
like SWAT team style.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.296
Like, it's got to be
something good,

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:18.431
you know,
something you remember.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:21.000
-Yeah. And how is that
going so far?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.701
-It was a flat "no"
on the chopper.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.637
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-We'll see.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.905
We'll see if we can
push them through.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.141
-I want to talk about
"Crikey! It's the Irwins."

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.575
-"Crikey!" Yeah, that's it.

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:33.245
-Second season is starting in
October -- next week.

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:35.548
Over 40 million people
are watching the show.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:36.983
-Oh, it has been incredible.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:40.152
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, thank you.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:44.824
-And what you do for
animals and for wildlife

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:45.924
is just amazing --
you and your family.

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:47.226
-Thank you very much.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.662
And, you know, a lot of the show
is kind of what we do

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.631
with our rescue work,
rehabilitation.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.999
So, rescuing wild animals,
giving them that

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:56.302
second chance at survival --
that's what we're all about.

00:03:56.302 --> 00:03:58.671
And we love what we get to do.
It really is incredible.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:03:59.738
-And just reminding everybody,

00:03:59.738 --> 00:04:01.307
yeah, what we're
fighting for here.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:03.609
-Exactly. Yeah.
We've only got one planet.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.211
-Yeah. Exactly. Right?

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.879
But you're following
in your dad's footsteps

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:07.947
and you are doing a great job.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:09.882
-Oh, I love it. I really do.
Thanks.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:14.053
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:17.924
-We actually got a photo
of you this season

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:21.427
and we compared it to
a photo of your dad

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.730
with the same croc, I believe.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:25.030
-Yeah, it's the exact same croc.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.833
-That's got to be --
That's just got to be amazing

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.102
when you see something
like that.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:30.403
If you can zoom in a little bit,
you can see --

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.537
-That was actually
the same croc.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:34.006
That's Murray.
And we're both feeding it.

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:36.242
And I actually hadn't seen
this photo before,

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.110
so that was completely
by chance.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.413
And, you know, that's why we do
what we do, you know,

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.914
is to continue that legacy.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.417
And, you know, with all the
conservation properties

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:47.653
we have all over the world,
all the conservation projects,

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:49.421
the wildlife hospital,
everything we do at the zoo --

00:04:49.421 --> 00:04:50.923
it's to make sure
that everything

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.658
dad fought for continues.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:56.095
-Well, he's looking down.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:59.031
He's looking down
and he's very, very, buddy.

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.233
-Thank you very much.
-Very proud. I love you, buddy.

00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:02.434
-Robert Irwin, everybody.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:05.071
Season 2 of
"Crikey! It's the Irwins"

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:08.374
premieres October 5th at
8:00 p.m. on Animal Planet.

